</Field Guns Equipment>

<overview>
<p>Jump infantry platoons equip their troops with personal jump packs that allow short powered hops across broken terrain, over walls, and onto rooftops. This vertical mobility gives jump platoons access to positions that foot and motorized infantry cannot reach, making them particularly effective in urban combat, mountainous terrain, and defensive operations where elevation matters. The trade-off is cost and logistics: jump packs require fuel, maintenance, and trained operators, limiting the number of jump platoons a garrison command can field compared to standard foot formations.</p><p>Supplementing their primary arms with shoulder-launched short-range missile systems, these platoons carry enough anti-armor punch to threaten light vehicles and damage exposed BattleMech components at close range. A rare few are equipped with heavier armor than is commonly found, allowing these teams to assault well protected objectives and hold critical positions as long as possible.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date selected as Light SRM common date
